WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.300
A show is chosen.

2
00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.736
An exhibition is not everything you made.

3
00:00:03.896 --> 00:00:09.376
It is the works that fit a theme, put in an order, with labels that say what each one is.

4
00:00:09.536 --> 00:00:12.508
Every choice is made for the person who comes to look.

5
00:00:13.208 --> 00:00:14.462
Height and space.

6
00:00:14.622 --> 00:00:20.705
Hang work so its middle is at eye height, and leave space between pieces so one does not shout over another.

7
00:00:20.865 --> 00:00:24.023
A sculpture goes on a plinth, where people can walk round it.

8
00:00:24.723 --> 00:00:26.070
Praise and guidance.

9
00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:33.986
Grade 4 feedback does two things: it celebrates what is really there, and it tells the artist what to try next.

10
00:00:34.146 --> 00:00:38.232
'Your stitches are even, hang it lower so people can see them' does both.

11
00:00:38.392 --> 00:00:39.925
'It is nice' does neither.

12
00:00:40.625 --> 00:00:41.925
Look back at the year.

13
00:00:42.085 --> 00:00:47.101
Your journal holds the whole year: the first wobbly drawing and the last careful one.

14
00:00:47.261 --> 00:00:52.973
Reading it back is how you see how far you have come, and how you decide what to work on next.
